  "mistake_move": "2...g5",
  "prompt": "White to move. Black has moved the f- and g-pawns. Can you checkmate in one?",
  "hints": [
   "Look at the diagonal from your queen towards Black's king.",
   "Nothing can block on f7 or g6."
  ],
  "notes": {
   "1...f6": "This takes the f6 square from the knight and opens the diagonal e8-h5.",
   "2...g5": "Now nothing can block the diagonal between h5 and e8.",
   "3.Qh5#": "Checkmate: the king can't move, and nothing can capture the queen or block the check."
  },
  "explanation": "The f- and g-pawns shelter the king. After ...f6 and ...g5 the diagonal from h5 to e8 is wide open, and 3.Qh5 is checkmate. It's the mirror image of Fool's Mate. Early in the game, be very careful with the pawns next to your king.",
