  "key_move": "4.Qh5+",
  "mistake_move": "3...fxe5",
  "prompt": "White to move. You gave up a knight. Now use the weakened diagonal to Black's king.",
  "hints": [
   "Black's f-pawn no longer shields the king.",
   "A queen check on the long diagonal forks king and more."
  ],
  "notes": {
   "2...f6": "This defends e5 with a pawn, but it takes away the king's best defender and opens the diagonal h5-e8.",
   "3...fxe5": "Taking the knight lets the white queen in.",
   "4.Qh5+": "Check along the diagonal that f6 opened.",
   "5.Qxe5+": "Check again, and the rook on h8 is attacked too.",
   "6.Qxh8": "White wins the rook and ends up with more material."
  },
  "explanation": "The pawns in front of your king are its shield. Moving the f-pawn (2...f6) and then taking the knight (3...fxe5) let the white queen in with check. Black should have played 3...Qe7. Think twice before moving the pawns next to your king.",
